<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm12-wenchang ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 12 / SatNet LEO group (Hainan Commercial LC-2, Wenchang) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Event times: CALT TYPICAL LM-12 sequence (Y7, SF-18 handbook) via https://sat.huijiwiki.com/wiki/长征十二号: S1 cutoff 196.315 s, sep 198.315 s, fairing 209.015 s, S2 first-burn cutoff 622.505 s.
Azimuth 141.27 deg: great-circle bearing from pad to centroid 9.108N 119.275E (1471 km) of NOTAM RPHI B5920/26 / HYDROPAC 3200/26 area (https://space-notices.com/entry/launch-long-march-12-satnet-leo-group-tbd); implies i~53.9 deg.
Orbit unpublished: S2 first-cutoff altitude 300 km circular ASSUMED (= Wikipedia 10 t to 300 km LEO reference, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_March_12). Payload: 9 SatNet LEO satellites per LL2.
T0: LL2 NET 2026-11-08T20:25:00Z (window 20:17-20:47Z = Sun 8 Nov 12:25 pm PST).
Altitude knots (t s: km; times published typical sequence, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times, final = assumed orbit): 0:0, 196.315:103.2, 198.315:105.9, 209.015:119.8, 622.505:300
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.452 km/s (circular v at 300 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+622.505 s. File ends at final cutoff.
Pad (LL2): 19.597550N 110.936481E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=141.27 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-08T20:25:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
